Origin
AAD began as a fork of cadcraft (https://github.com/storytold/cadcraft),
Copyright (c) 2026 ArtCraft Team and the CADCraft contributors, which is licensed under the same
MIT OR Apache-2.0 terms. That copyright and licence notice is kept in LICENSE-MIT. The 3D,
parametric-constraint and mechanical-engineering parts of that project were removed in this fork.

Third-party software
Every Rust dependency is listed with its licence in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md (generated by
`cargo xtask licenses`, which also fails the quality gate on a dependency whose licence is not on the
project's allow list). One is under a weak-copyleft licence: the acadrust crate (DWG reading,
https://github.com/hakanaktt/acadrust) is licensed under the Mozilla Public License 2.0 and is used
unmodified as a separate library (crates/dwg); its source is available from crates.io and the
repository above. No GPL, LGPL or AGPL code is linked or copied (CLAUDE.md, clean-room rules).

Optional components that are not part of this repository and are added when a release is packaged:
- IBM Plex fonts (https://github.com/IBM/plex), Copyright (c) IBM Corp., SIL Open Font License 1.1
  (Reserved Font Name "Plex"). The files are installed in the application's fonts folder together
  with their licence texts and a SOURCES.txt that records the release and a hash of each file.
- The assistant's language model (Qwen3-1.7B, GGUF quantisation) when the build includes the
  assistant. The model is published by its authors under the Apache License 2.0; the licence that
  applies is the one in the model card of the file that is shipped. It runs through llama.cpp
  (MIT License, via the llama-cpp-2 crate). The model never leaves the computer.
- Fonts from the optional craft-fonts build input (CRAFT_FONTS_DIR), when used, are listed in its
  own ATTRIBUTION.md, each under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.

Assets
Every bundled asset is original to AAD (icons, drafting font, hatch patterns and linetypes are drawn
or defined in code). The per-file list is in ATTRIBUTION.md.

